title: 'Decided by Jeff: a replaced root shows its own folders, as a fresh view of it would.'
pid: e7b8e4fd-3a44-4a48-a6a4-8865b53e4d47
body: |2-
  The first build left the original's folders under the replacement,
  each member drawn noWarrant. Told so of the containers folder, Jeff
  wrote: "Let's replace it with one that's accurate." That was built
  first (0cde1222); the other folders followed the same day on Top's
  mission, Jeff having said nothing against it, so that Top's mail to
  Jeff seen from Jeff's perspective shows the count of what Jeff has not
  touched. Now, whenever 'substitute_roots' re-points a root to another
  node, every folder the old root held vanishes, and in its place stand
  the same kinds of folder for the node now shown, empty, for their own
  visits to fill ('redraw_folders' in 'server/refresh/visit.rs'); the
  root asks for its containers folder as a fresh view's root does, and,
  if it was editable, to be extended as one, which adds its default
  subscribee folder, with its count, where it subscribes. Switching back
  draws the original's again, the same way. Consequences, each decided:
  - The folders and their members get new viewnode IDs at every switch;
    point inside one moves to the root. A folder hidden in the root
    stays hidden; its members are drawn anew, unfolded, so a search hit
    found by an alias, whose other folders' members the search folded,
    shows them open after a switch.
  - A root whose containers folder the user had removed gets one again:
    the view was drawn for another node.
  - A folder is redrawn with the other side of its relation, as a
    request for the relation draws both: under a search hit, L's
    overrider folder becomes J's overridden folder, and back.
contains:
